{
  "description": "Editor frame rate with 500 items: summary of two runs of scripts/measure-fps.ts (pnpm measure:fps); the full harness output, with per-frame intervals, is not included",
  "notes": [
    "Capped runs follow headless Chromium's vsync, a synthetic 60 Hz clock, not the built-in display, so they read 60 fps in every configuration (meanFps 59.98 to 60.01).",
    "refreshRateHz is the harness's blank-page probe: 1000 divided by the median frame interval. Frame timestamps come in 0.1 ms steps, so each of the 4,800 intervals in the capped windows is 16.5, 16.6, 16.7 or 16.8 ms, with a median of 16.7 ms (1000 / 16.7 = 59.88, calculated) and a mean of 16.666 ms (60.00 Hz, calculated). The probe's 59.88 Hz comes from that rounding, not from a slow clock.",
    "Uncapped with instancing on, the closing GPU read-back waited 944.6 to 1935.6 ms (gpuDrainMs): the page issued frames faster than the GPU drew them, so only meanFps includes the GPU work in those windows, and their medianFps, medianFrameMs and frame-time percentiles follow the requestAnimationFrame clock. With instancing off it waited 24.3 to 26 ms.",
    "The Apple M2 Pro is far faster than the integrated graphics the design targets, so these numbers compare configurations; they do not show performance on that target."
  ],
